    word-for-word.
  </p>

  <p>
    Most "best tools" content online is written to a formula: skim the
    landing page, restate the feature list, add a comparison table, publish.
    HoneyTools is an attempt to do the opposite.
  </p>

  <h2>How Reviews Here Work</h2>
  <p>
    Every review is written by someone who has actually used the tool —
    not a summary of what the tool claims to do. That means real opinions
    about what's genuinely good, what's overrated, and who a tool is
    actually a bad fit for, even when that's less flattering than a
    typical "review."
  </p>

  <h2>Affiliate Links Never Affect Rankings</h2>
  <p>
    Some posts include affiliate links, and they're always disclosed. But
    a tool being covered here — or being recommended over another — is
    never influenced by whether an affiliate program exists for it. If a
    tool isn't worth using, that gets said plainly, commission or not.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to Go Next</h2>
  <p>
    Head to <a href="/reviews/">Reviews</a> for individual tool write-ups,
    or <a href="/guides/">Guides</a> for more practical, how-to content.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
